From 75d8e9953697972782df1c121dc0738410124d16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shahriar Iravanian <siravan@svtsim.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:21:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] rusticol: symjit-compiled executors on the pacman
 runner (ops 13 and 14; local, e2e)

A symjit contribution or finalization executor keeps the SHA-256 of its plane application and
reports its binding (evaluator/symjit_direct.rs, pacman::binding). With a runner that has the
kernel (capability bit 2, pacman_recurrence_v1_symjit_kernel), the hook encodes its row groups as
an op 14 binding and op 13 rows; the kernels' model parameters and literals go in scale slots
after the source masses, refreshed on every call. The pacman feature now needs f64-symjit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
